>> title: Crab Rangoon
>> category: Dumplings & Rolls
>> tags: crab, cream cheese, deep-fry, appetiser, american-chinese
>> counters: Takeout Counter
>> aka: crab rangoon, crab ragoon, cream cheese wonton, crab puffs, 蟹角
>> pairs-with: sweet-and-sour-sauce
>> servings: 6
>> time: 45 min
>> slack: narrow — the seal has to be complete: a wrapper that opens in the oil dumps cream cheese into the fryer and the batch after it tastes of that
>> step.1: beat smooth, no lumps
>> step.2: fold in, chill 20 min
>> step.3: fill and seal, a teaspoon each
>> step.4: fry 350°F (175°C) 3 min, drain

Beat @cream cheese{8%oz}(225 g; softened) with @sugar{2%tsp}, @garlic powder{1/4%tsp}, @Worcestershire sauce{1/2%tsp}, and @kosher salt{1/4%tsp} until it is perfectly smooth — a lump will burst the wrapper in the oil.

Fold @crab meat{6%oz}(170 g; picked over) and @scallions{3}(thinly sliced) into @&(~1)cheese{}, then ~chill{20%min} so it firms up enough to handle.

Fill @wonton wrappers{24}(thin, square) with a teaspoon of @&(~1)filling{} each, wetting all four edges with @water{2%Tbs} and pressing the corners together into a purse with no air trapped inside.

Fry @&(~1)parcels{} six at a time in @peanut oil{4%cups}(950 mL; at 350°F/175°C) for ~fry{3%min}, turning once, until blistered and gold, then drain them on a rack.
